# WISEPACK machine-local settings — TEMPLATE. Safe to commit.
#
#     cp config/local.env.example config/local.env
#
# `config/local.env` is git-ignored on purpose: it holds values that describe
# THIS host and must not travel with the repository. Nothing here is a secret in
# the cryptographic sense, but a published SSH port is free reconnaissance, so
# the real value stays out of tracked files, README examples, test fixtures,
# generated artefacts and logs.
#
# Resolution order used by the launchers and helper scripts:
#   1. an already-exported WISEPACK_SSH_PORT (an explicit override always wins)
#   2. config/local.env
#   3. the SERVER-side port from $SSH_CONNECTION, when running inside an SSH
#      session — that is its fourth field
#   4. otherwise the scripts leave it unresolved and say so, rather than
#      assuming 22. Guessing a port produces a port-forward command that
#      silently connects somewhere else, or nowhere.

# The SSH port of THIS server, used to build port-forwarding examples for the
# Isaac Sim WebRTC stream.
WISEPACK_SSH_PORT=YOUR_SSH_PORT
